Subject: [PATCH 0006/9006] avp-proxy: F2 ABI translation for the avp-own prebuilt decode handlers

The userspace sends AUDDEC_INIT/VIDDEC_INIT with the 2025-padded sizes
(632/664); the SDK Jul-2024 prebuilts in the AVP expect the legacy words
(608/644). The pads are trailing fields, so rewriting the command size
resizes the forwarded payload correctly in both directions.

Evidence F1c (2026-09-29): avp-own-96h (standalone type + WDT) boots and
stays alive; kernel boots; logo renders; menu hangs at frogui init - the
RPC to the decode handlers never answers (word mismatch).
---
--- a/drivers/hcdrivers/avp-proxy/avp-proxy.c
+++ b/drivers/hcdrivers/avp-proxy/avp-proxy.c
@@ -557,6 +557,28 @@
 	unsigned long parg_avp = 0;
 	int sz = _IOC_SIZE(cmd);
 	int dir = _IOC_DIR(cmd);
+	unsigned int fwd_cmd = cmd;
+
+	/* 0006 (F2, clase D 2026-09-29): ABI translation for the avp-own
+	 * prebuilt decode handlers. The userspace (factory libhudi.so +
+	 * our recompiled stack, built against the 2025-padded headers)
+	 * sends AUDDEC_INIT/VIDDEC_INIT with sizes 632/664; the SDK
+	 * Jul-2024 prebuilts in the AVP expect the legacy words 608/644
+	 * (0x82600301/0x82840400). The pads are trailing fields
+	 * (auddec.h:103, vidmp.h:208): the legacy struct == the first
+	 * 608/644 bytes, so rewriting the size resizes the forwarded
+	 * payload correctly in both directions. Only the forwarding word
+	 * changes — the local pre/postproc switches keep matching the
+	 * userspace word. Evidence: F1c boot test 2026-09-29 — the
+	 * avp-own-96h boots and stays alive (standalone type + WDT), the
+	 * kernel boots, the logo renders, and the menu hangs at frogui
+	 * init: the RPC to the decode handlers never answers. */
+	if (cmd == AUDDEC_INIT)
+		fwd_cmd = _IOC(_IOC_DIR(cmd), _IOC_TYPE(cmd), _IOC_NR(cmd),
+			       608);
+	else if (cmd == VIDDEC_INIT)
+		fwd_cmd = _IOC(_IOC_DIR(cmd), _IOC_TYPE(cmd), _IOC_NR(cmd),
+			       644);
 
 	if (sz > 0) {
 		parg_avp = (unsigned long)kzalloc(sz, GFP_KERNEL);
@@ -579,7 +601,7 @@
 		goto err_ret;
 	}
 
-	ret = avp_ioctl(fpriv->avp_fd, cmd, parg_avp);
+	ret = avp_ioctl(fpriv->avp_fd, fwd_cmd, parg_avp);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		goto err_ret;
 	}
